    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pairs\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nMy expected behavior is:\r\n\r\n`((|))`: Pressing `<BS>` twice will delete all parentheses.\r\n`(()|)`: Pressing `<BS>` twice will only remove the inner parentheses.\r\n\r\nThe current behavior is:\r\n\r\n`(()|)`: Pressing `<BS>` twice results in `(`\r\n\r\nIs it possible to achieve this behavior? Alternatively, I would like to delete the closing parenthesis `(|)` only when it is auto-paired *just now*, rather than whenever there are matching parentheses around the cursor. But I don't know how to do that.\r\n\r\nThank you!",
