            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThe first one requires figuring out whether parenthesis are balanced or not. This is out of scope of 'mini.pairs' as it deliberately works [only based on character to the left and character to the right](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/77533e69cc4fadb7f4c25f23255ae0890a058818/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L9-L10) (for performance reasons).\r\n\r\nThe second one is quite tricky to implement as it requires tracking being started *every time* a pair is inserted, which is out of scope (again for performance).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
